STARTER - Simple disTributed smaRT controllER

1. OVERVIEW
===========

STARTER (Simple disTributed smaRT controllER) is a core system for 
distributed control environments. It is designed to coordinate multiple 
nodes through a lightweight and robust communication stack:

* Discovery: Uses mDNS (Multicast DNS) for automatic peer discovery.
* Communication: Uses D-Bus for reliable inter-process communication (IPC).

For more detailed information, please consult the technical manual in the
'doc' directory (sources: starter-core.texi; PDF: doc/starter-core.pdf).
Rebuild the PDF with: make -C doc pdf

2. PREREQUISITES
================

To build and run STARTER, you need the following dependencies:
* GLib 2.0 (libglib2.0-dev)
* D-Bus (libdbus-1-dev)
* Avahi / mDNS stack (libavahi-client-dev, libavahi-glib-dev)
* MySQL / MariaDB client (default-libmysqlclient-dev or equivalent)
* Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool, pkg-config)
* Texinfo (makeinfo) — required by configure; also used to build the manual

On Debian/Ubuntu (example):
  sudo apt install build-essential autoconf automake libtool pkg-config \
    libglib2.0-dev libavahi-client-dev libavahi-glib-dev \
    default-libmysqlclient-dev texinfo

3. BUILDING FROM SOURCE
=======================

From a git checkout, regenerate the Autotools files then configure:

    $ autoreconf -fi
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    $ sudo make install

Optional remote debug server (GDBus):

    $ ./configure --enable-debug-server

Do not use a project-specific autogen script; autoreconf picks the host
autoconf/automake/libtool versions correctly.

4. CONFIGURATION
================

STARTER is designed to run as a systemd service. Initial setup requires 
defining node identities and mDNS service names.

    $ sudo systemctl enable --now starter.service

